Article 3
Paragraph (1) what is meant by "physical violence" is any act that results in pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and or causes death. What is meant by "psychological violence" is an act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and or severe psychological suffering to a person. What is meant by "sexual violence" is any act in the form of sexual harassment, forced sexual intercourse, forced unnatural or unwanted sexual intercourse, forced sexual intercourse with others for commercial purposes and or certain purposes. What is meant by "exploitation" includes: acts that exploit a child economically or sexually with the intention of benefiting oneself or others;
acts with or without the consent of the victim that
b.
include but are not limited to prostitution, forced labor or services, slavery or similar practices, oppression, extortion, utilization of physical, sexual, reproductive organs, or unlawfully removing or transplanting organs and/or body tissues or utilizing the labor or ability of a person by another party to obtain benefits both material and immaterial.
c. all forms of utilization of sexual organs or other body organs of the victim to obtain benefits, including but not limited to all activities of prostitution or sexual abuse.
What is meant by "trafficking in persons" is the act of recruitment, transportation, harboring, sending, transfer, or receipt of a person by threat of violence, use of violence, abduction, confinement, forgery, fraud, abuse of power or position of vulnerability, debt bondage or giving payment or benefits, so as to obtain consent from the person holding control over that other person, whether conducted within the country or between countries, for the purpose of exploitation or resulting in a person being exploited.
What is meant by "Household Neglect" is: an act that results in the non-fulfillment of a child's needs properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social;
b. an act of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate;
c. an act that neglects a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person;
d. an act that results in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person. What is meant is deviant behavior of children such as the use of glue/aibon which can cause children to feel addicted or intoxicated because they are invited by their friends, and deviation towards free sexual behavior or use of illicit goods.
